WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.543
Now we combine several tables in one query The first
join moves

00:00:05.569 --> 00:00:10.585
from patients to admissions using patient ID Because
the question is about

00:00:10.611 --> 00:00:16.168
admission detail an INNER JOIN is reasonable The
second join moves

00:00:16.194 --> 00:00:20.115
from each admission to the attending staff member
using attending staff ID

00:00:21.052 --> 00:00:23.999
We use LEFT JOIN so an admission can remain even if
the

00:00:24.026 --> 00:00:30.430
staff reference is missing Run the query and inspect
the path Each

00:00:30.443 --> 00:00:37.042
result row represents an admission enriched with
patient and clinician information This

00:00:37.069 --> 00:00:41.187
is a good example of joining through documented
relationships rather than connecting

00:00:41.213 --> 00:00:46.992
tables simply because they share some
similar-looking column When a query becomes

00:00:47.018 --> 00:00:52.166
longer draw or state the path before writing SQL
Patient to admission

00:00:53.074 --> 00:00:58.060
Admission to staff That sequence makes the role of
each join easier

00:00:58.087 --> 00:01:03.610
to verify Also keep checking the grain Adding

00:01:03.636 --> 00:01:07.320
the staff table should not create extra rows because
one attending staff

00:01:07.347 --> 00:01:09.584
ID points to at most one staff member
